.TH PUBLIC_KEY 1 "September 2025" "MyWallet Toolkit 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
public_key \- Bitcoin public key generator from secp256k1 private keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B public_key.sh
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-f 
.IR format ]
.RB [ \-h ]
[\fIPRIVATE_KEY_HEX\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B public_key.sh
generates Bitcoin public keys from secp256k1 private keys using elliptic curve cryptography. It supports both compressed and uncompressed public key formats and includes proper validation of private key values against the secp256k1 curve order.

The tool performs elliptic curve point multiplication to derive the corresponding public key from a given private key, following Bitcoin's cryptographic standards.

.B WARNING:
This tool is designed for educational and testing purposes only. Never use this script for production Bitcoin wallets or real funds. For actual Bitcoin storage, always use hardware wallets or certified software solutions.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode. Suppress warnings and informational output.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode. Show progress and processing steps.
.TP
.B \-f \fIformat\fR
Specify the output format. Supported values:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
.B both
- Output both compressed and uncompressed formats (default)
.IP \(bu 4
.B compressed
- Output only compressed public key (33 bytes)
.IP \(bu 4
.B uncompressed
- Output only uncompressed public key (65 bytes)
.RE
.TP
.B \-h
Show help message and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate both compressed and uncompressed public keys:
.nf
echo 'a1b2c3d4e5f678901234567890123456a1b2c3d4e5f678901234567890123456' | ./public_key.sh
.fi

.TP
Generate only compressed public key:
.nf
./public_key.sh -f compressed a1b2c3d4e5f678901234567890123456a1b2c3d4e5f678901234567890123456
.fi

.TP
Complete pipeline from mnemonic to public key:
.nf
echo "word1 word2 ... word12" | ./privatekey.sh -q | head -2 | tail -1 | ./public_key.sh -f compressed
.fi

.TP
Verbose mode showing processing steps:
.nf
echo 'private_key_hex' | ./public_key.sh -v -f both
.fi

.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B both format (default)
Outputs two lines:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Compressed public key (33 bytes, 66 hex characters)
.IP 2. 4
Uncompressed public key (65 bytes, 130 hex characters)
.RE

.TP
.B compressed format
Outputs compressed public key starting with 02 or 03
.br
Example: 02a1b2c3d4e5f678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456

.TP
.B uncompressed format
Outputs uncompressed public key starting with 04
.br
Example: 04a1b2c3d4e5f678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456a1b2c3d4e5f678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456

.SH INPUT FORMAT
.TP
.B Private Key Format
The tool accepts secp256k1 private keys in hexadecimal format:
.IP \(bu 4
Length: Exactly 64 hexadecimal characters (32 bytes)
.IP \(bu 4
Range: Must be between 1 and the secp256k1 curve order
.IP \(bu 4
Characters: 0-9, a-f, A-F

.SH TECHNICAL DETAILS
.SS Elliptic Curve Cryptography
The tool uses the secp256k1 elliptic curve as specified in Bitcoin:
.IP \(bu 4
.B Curve equation: 
y² = x³ + 7 (mod p)
.IP \(bu 4
.B Prime field: 
p = 2²⁵⁶ - 2³² - 977
.IP \(bu 4
.B Curve order: 
n = FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFEBAAEDCE6AF48A03BBFD25E8CD0364141

.SS Key Generation Process
.IP 1. 4
Validate private key is within valid range (1 < k < n)
.IP 2. 4
Perform elliptic curve point multiplication: Q = k × G
.IP 3. 4
Generate compressed format (33 bytes): 02/03 + x-coordinate
.IP 4. 4
Generate uncompressed format (65 bytes): 04 + x-coordinate + y-coordinate

.SS Compression Methods
.IP \(bu 4
.B Compressed
Stores only x-coordinate with parity bit (02 for even y, 03 for odd y)
.IP \(bu 4
.B Uncompressed
Stores complete coordinates with 04 prefix

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B openssl
Required for elliptic curve operations (version 3.x recommended)
.TP
.B xxd
Required for hexadecimal conversions
.TP
.B bc
Required for mathematical operations

.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.IP \(bu 4
Private keys must be cryptographically random
.IP \(bu 4
Private keys are validated against secp256k1 curve order
.IP \(bu 4
Tool rejects invalid private key values (0, negative, or >= curve order)
.IP \(bu 4
No private key material is logged in verbose mode

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, malformed private key, or execution error

.SH STANDARDS
.TP
.B SEC 2
Recommended Elliptic Curve Domain Parameters
.TP
.B ANSI X9.62
Public Key Cryptography for the Financial Services Industry
.TP
.B Bitcoin Core
Reference implementation standards

